From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:08:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibJS: Look past call, apply and Reflect.apply for a
 function's caller

A sloppy function's caller property gave null when the function was
called through Function.prototype.call or apply, or Reflect.apply, as
the frame below its own is that of the built-in. These call their
target as a tail call (PrepareForTailCall()), so the function that
called them is the caller, as in V8, SpiderMonkey and JavaScriptCore.

Ext JS finds the methods it overrides this way, as callParent() calls
callOverrideParent() through apply(), and that reads caller.caller.
Without this, Ext JS 6 apps such as the web UI of Proxmox VE threw
when they started, and showed an empty page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
